  "name": "restart-then-wrap-16",
  "description": "Six 30-minute intervals (18 entries) into a memory of 16 slots, so the ring has already wrapped once (marker at entry 17) and is persisted with storage fs; the instance is dropped and a new one loads the file (restartAfterEntry = 18). beforeRestart: status and the transfer from the oldest announced entry. afterRestart: the transfer from the oldest announced entry right after the reload. Then two more intervals (six entries) are added: the first entry after a restart into a full ring inserts a second reference-time marker. historyStatus and historyEntries are after them, in order: 0, the oldest announced entry, the newest entry, one past the newest.",
