    "entries": "every entry fed to fakegato-history addEntry({ time, power }) in this order: time is Unix seconds at the end of its 10-minute slot (start + 600 k), watts is the power given, deciwatts = watts * 10 is the 16-bit field value",
    "restartAfterEntry": "null, or the number of entries after which the instance was dropped and a new one loaded the persisted file",
    "beforeRestart": "null, or historyStatus, historyEntries and state read before the restart",
    "afterRestart": "null, or historyEntries and state read right after the reload, before any further entry",
    "historyStatus": "E863F116 bytes (hex, little-endian fields) as published after the last entry",
    "historyEntries": "in replay order on one running instance: for each History Request, the address requested, the exact E863F11C bytes written (hex: 01 14, u32 address, 00 00) and every E863F117 read (hex) until the terminator 00",
    "state": "the library counters after the last entry: firstEntry, lastEntry, usedMemory, refTime (first entry time minus epoch), initialTime"
